## 席位核对

ACCEPT · seat `domain:ui#4` · `session_01QsR2jTfvjNTaR29ehLk26T` · 2026-10-27T17:19Z · head `377ee2e4ec2bf5e4c5280d52341bce2d84aa5188`

1. **Shape:** draft, base `main`, first line `Fixes #26703`. `Clause-②: no` and `Metadata-protocol: none` match the claim (6445102551) and its amendment (6447933965), in the body and in the changeset (`@object-ui/app-shell` and `@object-ui/i18n` patch). Seven files, all inside the amended surface: `block-config.ts` (one `list-view` entry), `@object-ui/i18n` studio namespace `en.ts` / `zh.ts` (three labels each, beside the other `engine.inspector.pageBlock.*` rows that PR #26780 moved there), three test files beside, one root changeset. The branch merged main (`a06f1d92`) to pick that move up. No `packages/spec/**`, server or plugin-list change, and no new key.
2. **Premise, measured:** the seat read the diff. On main, `BLOCK_CONFIG` had no `list-view` row, so a selected list block showed no typed fields. The new row writes `dataSource.object` (object-picker), `dataSource.view` (text) and `dataSource.limit` (number, literal placeholder `5`, the capped list's own count from #26613), all `at: 'dataSource'` like `element:repeater`. All three are `ElementDataSourceSchema` members, so the schema-parity test judges them. The new test drives the real inspector on a spec-parsed page and asserts the patch lands on `dataSource`, never `properties`. Ablation of the entry turned its 4 cases red; restored.
3. **Gates, pinned to the head:** check-runs at `377ee2e4`: 52 total, 43 success, 9 skipped, 0 failed (Test UI 14/16 passes on this head; the two reds at `069c0195` were #26692's studio zh-title test, not this diff) · `check-governed-merges --pr 26793`: not governed. `mergeable_state`: clean.
4. **Accepted deviations:**
   - `PANEL_WITHOUT_PALETTE` in `block-config.test.ts` (a test file beside the surface): a one-row, self-deleting exemption from "a block with a panel is a block the palette offers", with its reason (published pages place `list-view`). Offering the block is a product change beyond this card;
   - the PR body still names the app-shell `i18n.ts` for the labels; the amendment records the move, since no relay op edits a PR body;
   - View is a text box, since the inspector has no saved-view picker kind; an unknown view still fails loudly at render;
   - the `scripts/` vitest leg timed out one tree-scan case (`check-vi-mock-inherit`) at 15 s under contention; that file re-ran alone 83/83 and touches nothing in this diff. Local at `377ee2e4`: 34 derived gates, 34 run, 0 NOT-MEASURED; touched tests 103/103; `check:i18n-designer-parity`, app-shell and i18n type-check exit 0.
5. **Out of scope:** the open question (offer `list-view` in the palette) is filed as #26794 with the thread's recommendation A (add it to `BLOCK_TYPE_META`, then drop the exemption row). `Skills-docs:` is not owed.
6. **Prose face, checked sentence by sentence against the diff:** each changeset claim matches a hunk and a test:
   - three controls writing `dataSource.object/view/limit`, hint `5` when empty;
   - labels in en and zh (the zh case);
   - no new key, nothing an author wrote changes, the palette still does not offer `list-view` (the exemption row).

**Landing:** no contract review is owed (no published schema, no governed text, `Clause-②: no`). The seat marks the PR ready and arms auto-merge. On MERGED, `Fixes #26703` closes the card.
